# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-14, F18); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: someone who likes every point of the screen used turns on soleFloatTakesDesktop.
# Notes floats alone beside Safari and takes the whole Desktop; when Mail opens, Notes is its
# old self again; when Mail closes, it takes the Desktop again; once resized by hand it is left alone.
# Reference: T21.
open Safari
open Notes
dock 101 left
set soleFloatTakesDesktop true
expect floating 102
expect left-of 101 102
# The Desktop framed: a window that takes the Desktop fills the view.
desktop
expect camera desktop
expect fills 102
back
# It goes out of view and comes back with the Desktop, like any floating window.
zoom 101
expect hidden 102
back
expect visible 102
# Company: both float at their own sizes, so Notes fits above Mail again.
open Mail 400x200
move 103 900 650 400 200
move 102 900 100 400 300
expect above 102 103
close 103
desktop
expect fills 102
back
# The user's hand wins: pulled shorter, it stays shorter.
pull 102 bottom -400
open Mail 400x200
move 104 900 650 400 200
expect above 102 104
dock 104 right
desktop
expect fills 102
back
# Back to a normal Mac: nothing is docked, so nothing is stretched.
float-all
close 101
close 104
desktop
expect floating 102
expect visible 102
